  "control_sha256": "0650397116219ba7ba4b7379a33770bd199c040c16c8fd6ecd553aacd7cec573",
  "scope": "One disposable kind v0.32.0 cluster with Kubernetes v1.36.1 and its bundled kindnet. Case-owned training, registry, inference, gateway, and untrusted namespaces use non-root BusyBox Pods and synthetic TCP/HTTP markers only. It measures no-policy baseline routes, then checks a job-label-scoped TCP interval using the CNI-supported endPort field, an adjacent out-of-range port, a same-port neighbor with another job label, an approved versus unapproved registry Pod, and inference ingress allowed only from a fixture gateway. No DNS, Services, external traffic, NCCL process, GPU, RDMA, production CNI, label authorization/integrity, real registry, application authentication, or production deployment is evaluated. A timeout is attributed to this controlled policy scenario only after healthy endpoints and a successful no-policy baseline; the NetworkPolicy API itself does not report a packet drop reason.",
